From: pdx203 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: gpu: per-process page tables

Every user client gets its own TTBR0 table and VM (NativeAdrenoGpuContext client spaces): a table in the live one's format
over [0, 4 GiB) with the five kernel buffers mapped at their addresses, the client's BOs in [64 MiB, 4 GiB). The submit
object switches the CP to the client's table with CP_SMMU_TABLE_UPDATE (a6xx_set_pagetable's sequence) when the next job runs
on another table, and a closing client's table goes only after the CP was switched back to the live one. The live and client
contexts accept a TTBR0 the device switched (ArmSmmu4KContextConfig.device_switched_ttbr0). Jobs remember their VM. A VM's
range table grows on demand (gm1: scattered 64 MiB blocks filled 131072 ranges). The board turns it on after its probe.

